+**A Git-first forge where repositories live on developer-run nodes, not in one platform's database.**
+
+ForkMesh is an early local-first developer platform for cloning, mirroring,
+reviewing, discussing, and preserving Git repositories across user-run nodes.
+Desktop nodes keep local bare Git mirrors, sign repository and collaboration
+metadata with local Ed25519 keys, and serve browse/clone traffic through a thin
+**mainnode** relay.
+
+The public network currently uses one Cloudflare Worker mainnode at
+`forkmesh.com` for discovery, encrypted rooms, signed inboxes, mirror health,
+Solana metadata, and the website. The mainnode is not canonical Git storage:
+Git history lives in local working copies and node mirrors. If an owner node goes
+offline, ForkMesh can keep a public repo cloneable from another healthy, synced
+mirror without changing the URL.
+
+ForkMesh works today for publishing and preserving public repos, browsing and
+cloning with stock Git, signed issues, patch-based pull requests, agent
+workflows, and experimental Solana-funded issues. It is not a GitHub drop-in
+replacement yet: multi-mainnode federation, production-ready push, hardened
+operations, audited money custody, and full forge ergonomics are still in
+progress.
+
+> **This is early, and that's the point.** If you show up now, you help shape the
+> protocol, test the trust model in public, and preserve repositories before the
+> mesh is large. Build a desktop node, mirror a project you care about, and file
+> the rough edges as signed issues.
 
