 ## Get Started
 
+
+### Git compatibility today
+
+| Operation | Stock Git? | Current status | Notes |
+|---|---:|---|---|
+| `git clone https://forkmesh.com/<owner>/<repo>` | Yes | Working for public repos | Uses smart HTTP `git-upload-pack`; requires a live source or healthy mirror. |
+| `git fetch` | Yes | Working for public repos | Same upload-pack path as clone. |
+| Web browse files/commits/diffs | Browser, not Git | Working when a host is live | The Worker forwards requests to a connected desktop node; it is not canonical Git storage. |
+| Mirror from GitHub/GitLab/Forgejo remotes | Yes, via desktop node | Working | The desktop node creates a local bare mirror with `git clone --mirror` / fetch. |
+| `git push` over ForkMesh | Stock Git transport, token required | Experimental / not production-ready | Receive-pack exists behind an owner-signed Basic-auth token; collaborator push, hardening, and continuous production E2E coverage are not done. |
+| Pull requests | No native Git ref PRs yet | Patch-based signed records | PRs are signed patch submissions, not hosted branch refs like GitHub. |
+| Git LFS | Unknown / not first-class | Do not rely on it | Document and test before claiming support. |
+| Private clone/browse | Git with token | Early/private-repo path | Requires signed view tokens; private repos do not use public mirror fallback. |
+
+### Coming from GitHub or GitLab
+
+Use ForkMesh as an extra mirror before making it your only forge:
+
+1. In the desktop node, use **+ Add** and paste an existing GitHub/GitLab/Forgejo clone URL.
+2. ForkMesh creates a local bare mirror and publishes signed catalog metadata to the mainnode.
+3. Keep your existing origin as canonical while testing ForkMesh browse/clone, signed issues, patch PRs, and agents.
+4. Share `https://forkmesh.com/<owner>/<repo>` for public browsing/cloning when at least one source or mirror node is online.
+5. Do not move regulated, private, or bounty-critical work fully onto ForkMesh until private repos, push, custody, and operations are audited.
+
+ForkMesh does not currently import GitHub issues, stars, Actions history,
+releases, branch-protection rules, or org permissions as first-class equivalents.
+Git history lives in your local mirror, not in the Worker.
+
 ### Desktop Node
 
