-## Security Notes
-
-- Relay chat payloads are encrypted client-side with AES-256-GCM; the relay only
-  sees ciphertext envelopes and cannot read room contents.
-- Profile and repository metadata are signed by the local Ed25519 identity.
+## Security Notes / MVP Threat Model
+
+ForkMesh currently protects against:
+
+- The mainnode forging signed profiles, repository metadata, issues, pull
+  requests, releases, and auth tokens without the relevant Ed25519 key.
+- A mirror silently serving a different public ref state when source-attested
+  repo-state pins exist.
+- The mainnode becoming canonical Git storage: clone, fetch, browse, and release
+  bytes are served from desktop nodes / node-local stores, not Worker-owned Git
+  history.
+
+ForkMesh does **not** yet protect against:
+
+- The public mainnode observing metadata such as account names, repository names,
+  timing, IP-level connection data, catalog records, and bounty metadata.
+- The public mainnode censoring, dropping, delaying, reordering, rate-limiting,
+  or losing catalog/inbox/room data.
+- Public/default room chat being secret from all app users: shared rooms use a
+  baked-in app key and should be treated as public rooms, even though the relay
+  stores/forwards ciphertext.
+- Malicious repository contents, untrusted Actions/agents, compromised local node
+  keys, or unsafe code reviewed by humans.
+- Legal/custody risk around Solana bounties.
+- Full multi-mainnode federation; the public network is one mainnode today.
+
+## How ForkMesh compares
+
+| Tool | Canonical Git storage | Network model | Push maturity | Best today |
+|---|---|---|---|---|
+| GitHub/GitLab | Platform-hosted repos | Centralized SaaS | Mature | Full-featured hosted forge |
+| Forgejo/Gitea | Self-hosted server repos | Self-hosted; federation emerging | Mature | Owning your forge server |
+| Radicle | Peer-held Git repos | P2P-first | Mature for its model | Sovereign Git collaboration |
+| ForkMesh | Desktop-node mirrors / local Git | One public mainnode today; federation planned | Experimental | Public repo preservation, mesh browsing/cloning, signed collaboration, agents, experimental bounties |
 
