+ForkMesh is a Git-first peer-to-peer forge. Desktop nodes hold working copies,
+local bare Git mirrors, and accepted issue/PR/discussion records. They talk
+through a thin **mainnode** relay for discovery, presence, encrypted room
+transport, signed inbox submissions, mirror-health indexing, and live
+clone/browse tunnels.
+
+The mainnode is not canonical Git storage. It should not store repository
+history or Git packfiles as the source of truth; it forwards Git smart-HTTP and
+browse requests to connected desktop nodes. It does store/serve operational
+metadata such as account bindings, catalog records, presence, encrypted room
+backlog, signed inbox records, and Solana/bounty metadata.
+
+Today the public network has one mainnode at `forkmesh.com`. Self-hosting a
+separate mainnode is possible with the reference Cloudflare Worker, but deployed
+multi-mainnode federation, catalog convergence, and cross-mainnode repository
+identity are not production realities yet.
+
+Reference implementation:
+- Mainnode relay/site: [`cloudflare_worker/`](../cloudflare_worker)
+- Desktop node: [`qt_client/`](../qt_client)
+- Public docs route: `https://forkmesh.com/docs/` (the static route also canonicalizes `/docs/` to `/docs`)
 
